Subject: [PATCH] fix(interaction): match native Bedrock offhand input

Do not interpret Java's automatic offhand fallback as a supported Bedrock
item or block action. Reject unsupported offhand block predictions with
block corrections and an acknowledgement, and resynchronize inventory
predictions without sending an offhand use transaction.

Native Minecraft Bedrock 1.26.51.1 captures using protocol 2193 and the
unmodified official Geyser 2.11.3 build 1247 established this behavior on
October 1, 2026. After publishing full fixture inventory snapshots and
verifying both hands in the native inventory, offhand dirt remained at
two blocks with no placement. Offhand rockets remained at three during
a valid glide, with no ordinary or packed item-use transaction. Mainhand
controls placed one block and consumed a rocket with a speed increase.

The protocol HandSlot field describes encoding, while allow_off_hand
describes inventory eligibility. Neither establishes active offhand use:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/minecraft/creator/reference/content/itemreference/examples/itemcomponents/minecraft_allow_off_hand
Shield use remains mapped to native Bedrock sneaking in the shield patch.
Keep captures and native screenshots private.
